\title{An order sent as a limit when one field of the live quote crosses a level}
\description{
It compares one value from the quote, not a computed indicator. The most useful is \code{average_price}, the day's volume-weighted average, because buying when the price comes back below the day's average cannot be written as a native stop. \code{trigger_price} here is the level, not the order's own trigger. It answers HTTP 202 with an \code{outcome} of \code{armed} and sends nothing to a broker until it fires, so keep the \code{parent_id} from the answer. Once it fires, its limit is held in UBI's virtual order book until the other side of the book reaches it, even if the price moves back, unless \code{hold_limits} is \code{FALSE}.

The order template's attributes are described on \code{SyntheticOrder}.
}
